//? Title: Online variance: actual Welford updates and finite precision
//? Subtitle: Original offset sweep, atomic chunk merging and paired covariance
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Derive actual streaming centered moments from two observations, then retain the
original seeded10000-value offset experiment and subsequent5000 paired
covariance observations. Computed update/merge records and a centered-wide
reference qualify the limits of numerical stability, including signal already
lost when shifted inputs are rounded.
)

\toc

> Centered moments instead of subtracting two large totals

For n accepted values, store the computed mean m_n and centered sum M2_n. Adding
x uses

$$ \delta=x-m_n, \qquad m_{n+1}=m_n+\frac{\delta}{n+1}, \qquad M2_{n+1}=M2_n+\delta(x-m_{n+1}). $$
\alttext(The new mean moves by the old-mean deviation divided by the new count, and the centered second moment increases by the product of deviations from the old and new means.)

Population variance is M2/n; sample variance is M2/(n−1) for n≥2. Empty
mean/variance and singleton sample variance return the historical0 convention,
rather than an asserted unbiased estimate from insufficient data. The centered
recurrence avoids the deliberate subtraction of a large squared mean from a
large raw second moment. It does not guarantee exact variance, accuracy
independent of offset, or recovery of input differences that binary64 has
already erased.

> Two hand-checkable actual additions

For[2,4], the second actual record has old mean2, delta2, new mean3, remaining
delta1 and M2 increment2. Its sample variance is2. The diagram and table use
canonical observations from the same atomic addition path used by ordinary
OnlineVariance::add().

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/online_variance_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::online_variance_trace({2, 4});
    auto &s = t.updates[1];
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("old", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual old count {}\nmean {} M2 {}", s.before.count,
                       s.before.mean, s.before.m2));
    d.node("update", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual x={} delta={}\nremaining delta={}", s.input,
                       double(s.delta), double(s.delta_after)));
    d.node("new", {16, 0},
           std::format("Actual new mean {}\nM2 {}", s.after.mean, s.after.m2));
    d.edge("old", "update").edge("update", "new");
    std::print("| actual input | count after | actual delta | actual new mean | actual remaining delta | " "actual M2 increment | actual M2 after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (auto &s : t.updates)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.input,
                   s.after.count, double(s.delta), s.after.mean,
                   double(s.delta_after), double(s.increment), s.after.m2);
    d.save_svg("build/online_variance_tiny.svg");
}
```
