> Chunk merging and the original covariance stream

For counts n_a,n_b, means m_a,m_b and centered sums A,B, write delta=m_b−m_a.
Combining the two complete states gives

$$ m=m_a+\delta\frac{n_b}{n_a+n_b}, \qquad M2=A+B+\delta^2\frac{n_an_b}{n_a+n_b}. $$
\alttext(The merged mean is count-weighted and the merged centered sum adds the two within-group sums plus a between-group correction.)

Empty-side merges copy or preserve the nonempty state. Source and destination
are snapshotted before mutation, so self-merge duplicates the original sample
state safely. In floating arithmetic, chunk grouping can change the last bits;
mergeability does not mean associativity or bitwise equality with a sequential
reduction.

The original RNG schedule continues after the10000 base draws with5000 pairs
x=normal(),y=3x+.5normal(). The paired accumulator updates means and the
centered cross-product sum, and uses marginal centered moments for correlation.
The figure displays the actual synthetic pairs, not fitted values or a claim
that the empirical correlation must equal its population value.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/online_variance_covariance.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto data = dm::algorithms::online_variance_demo_data();
    dm::algorithms::OnlineVariance left, right, serial;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < data.base.size(); ++i) {
        serial.add(data.base[i]);
        if (i < data.base.size() / 2)
            left.add(data.base[i]);
        else
            right.add(data.base[i]);
    }
    auto merge = left.merge_observed(right);
    dm::algorithms::OnlineCovariance covariance;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < data.x.size(); ++i)
        covariance.add(data.x[i], data.y[i]);
    std::print("| actual quantity | computed value |\n| --- | ---: |\n| left source count | {} |\n| right " "source count | {} |\n| actual merge delta | {:.12f} |\n| actual between-group M2 correction " "| {:.12f} |\n| merged sample variance | {:.12f} |\n| serial sample variance | {:.12f} |\n| " "paired observations | {} |\n| actual sample covariance | {:.12f} |\n| actual correlation | " "{:.12f} |\n",
               merge.left.count, merge.right.count, double(merge.delta),
               double(merge.correction), left.sample_variance(),
               serial.sample_variance(), covariance.count(),
               covariance.sample_covariance(), covariance.correlation());
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(data.x, data.y, "actual generated pairs",
             dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255});
    p.title("Original paired stream: y equals3x plus generated noise").x_label(
        "actual x observation").y_label("actual y observation").save_svg(
        "build/online_variance_covariance.svg");
}
```
